#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 161 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts a linear amplitude value to decibels
relative to full scale (dBFS). The conversion follows the formula dBFS
= 20 * log10(amplitude). An amplitude of 1 corresponds to 0 dBFS. Amplitudes
greater than 1 give positive dBFS values \, and amplitudes between
0 and 1 give negative dBFS values.;
#X text 240 184 Note: an amplitude value of 0 is converted to -144
dB (24-bit range).;
